# Build context for `gcloud builds submit`.
#
# WITHOUT this file gcloud falls back to .gitignore, which excludes
# data/processed/emb_cache/ — and the image would then re-embed 33.8k rows on
# every cold start. The serving index has to ship. Everything the container
# never opens is excluded instead, because the context is uploaded on each build.
.git/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Huge, and the container never reads it: the processed parquet is enough.
data/raw/

# Evaluation and authoring artefacts — not part of serving.
runs/
reports/
labelling/
tests/
eval/
deploy/
data/golden/
llm_queue/
*.md

# Experiment-only embedding caches. history_index_*.npy is the serving index
# and is deliberately NOT excluded.
data/processed/emb_cache/rq_*.npy
data/processed/emb_cache/discovery_*.npy
data/processed/emb_cache/eval_pool_*.npy
